      "content": "That's an interesting angle, I like the idea of them being more \"natural.\" To make that visual contrast really pop in the book, I want to get specific. Since they live in these harsh, wild lands, maybe they have certain physical features or skin tones that reflect that intense environment? Like, maybe their skin is deeply pigmented or scarred from the elements, or they have these very exotic, intense facial features that make them look different from the pale, soft-looking empire folk. Can you help me describe their physical appearance and some of those \"wilder\" cultural markers—like tattoos or jewelry—that would make them look more striking and unrefined compared to the empire?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
